1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:04,400
Hey, you may have noticed I'm running a bit behind on episodes recently.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:11,360
Well, I mentioned it at the end of the last episode with Tyler, but I'm taking a little back to school break here at Launched.

3
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:17,280
Like with many of you, I have kids going back to school right now in whatever capacity that means in your area.

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,640
This year is actually my oldest's first year kindergarten.

5
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:27,440
Plus, my wife is a teacher who's currently trying to figure out how to teach a five to six year olds through iPads and zoom calls.

6
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:35,920
So I decided to pull back on all my side project commitments to make sure I can dedicate as much time as possible to helping out with all this crazy stuff.

7
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,080
And so Launched is one of them those.

8
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,160
So don't worry, I'll be back.

9
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:48,320
Hopefully by next month, but to be honest, I'm not opening back up this commitment until I feel like we've gotten things figured out on the school front first.

10
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:52,080
So it's possible it'll be a while, but hopefully not.

11
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:59,920
So if you find yourself wanting stories from indie creators, I'd really recommend checking out the new Indie Dev Monday newsletter by Josh Holtz.

12
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:06,560
In a lot of ways, it's kind of like a readable version of this show, except it's weekly, and he interviews two devs every week.

13
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,560
So there's a whole lot more going on.

14
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:15,760
It's a really quick way to kind of bootstrap yourself into this community and learn about a lot of cool devs doing cool stuff.

15
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:19,840
He's six issues in currently, and so far I've been a really big fan.

16
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:24,560
So obviously I'll have a link to that in the show notes of this episode.

17
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:29,520
So anyway, I just wanted to give a quick heads up as to why you won't be seeing any new episodes for a little while.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,040
I'm not going anywhere.

19
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,840
I'm just taking a quick, hopefully quick, back to school break.

20
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:35,280
Stay safe, everybody.
